# bt-dialog: the real Bluetooth window (src/dialog_bt.c) over the real main
# screen. The path is the firmware's own: main_screen_start_app(ACTION_APP_BT) ->
# dialog_construct(dialog_bt) -> src/dialog_bt.c builds the header, the device
# table, the status line and the Scan/RX/Speaker/Auto/Close button row.
#
# UI-005: the historical defect was the dialog's status line ("no headphones, RX
# off") sitting on the old dialog geometry (DIALOG_H 372 / DIALOG_Y 108) and being
# covered by the bottom button row (which starts at 480 - 62). This fixture renders
# the window and scenario_settle codifies the metric: the status label's bottom has
# to end above the button row (y=418); if it drops below again the run stops
# instead of capturing a covered line green.
#
# The host has no btaudio-ctl: `system()` is wrapped to a no-op and the file the
# script would leave is seeded with a fixed device list (mocks/mock_btaudio.c), so
# the table draws a real row ("Living Room TV", headphones, not connected).
#
# Deterministic: the dialog reads the harness' virtual clock (get_time()), never the
# host's.

name bt-dialog
screen bt-dialog

seed 20

frequency_hz 14074000
tx_frequency_hz 14074000
fft_width_hz 384000

mode usb
vfo A
agc auto

split false
att false
pre false
atu false
ant 1

smeter_db -73

battery_v 12.1
external_v 13.8
battery_cap 76
charging false

rxtx rx
